---
/**
 * Right of withdrawal and complaints: the English counterpart of
 * `src/pages/otkaz-i-reklamacii.astro`.
 *
 * Two different rights that are routinely confused. Withdrawal is the 14-day
 * right for distance and off-premises contracts (Art. 50 ZZP, Directive
 * 2011/83/EU), with the exception in Art. 57, item 1 for a service fully
 * performed with prior express consent. That exception is the one that matters
 * for this business: the car is left and the work is done the same day.
 * A complaint is the separate right under Art. 123 et seq. ZZP.
 *
 * Same facts, same structure and the same effective date as the Bulgarian page.
 * The Bulgarian page is the legally binding one; the first paragraph says so.
 */
import Text from '../../layouts/Text.astro';
import { crumbSchema, bizRef } from '../../lib/seo';
import { BUSINESS as b } from '../../config/site';
import { LEGAL_EN, ROUTES } from '../../i18n';
import { dict } from '../../i18n/ui';

const path = '/en/returns/';
const bgPath = ROUTES.find((r) => r.en === path)!.bg;
const [, terms] = LEGAL_EN;
const t = dict('en');

const updated = '11 September 2026';
const address = `${b.address.streetEn}, ${b.address.cityEn} ${b.address.postalCode}`;

const site = Astro.site!.href.replace(/\/$/, '');
const schema = [
  bizRef(site, 'en'),
  crumbSchema(site, [{ href: '/en/', label: 'Home' }, { href: path, label: 'Withdrawal and complaints' }]),
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'WebPage',
    url: `${site}${path}`,
    name: 'Right of withdrawal and complaints',
    description: 'The statutory 14-day withdrawal period for distance contracts, when it lapses and how to file a complaint.',
    inLanguage: 'en',
    dateModified: '2026-09-11',
    about: { '@id': `${site}/#business` },
  },
];
---
<Text
  title="Withdrawal and complaints — PDK Tuning"
  description="When the 14-day right of withdrawal applies and when it lapses, how to file a complaint and how soon we refund. With a model withdrawal form and address."
  heading="Withdrawal and complaints"
  lead="Two different rights that are often confused: withdrawal means “I have changed my mind”, a complaint means “the work is not right”. This page says which one applies when."
  updated={updated}
  schema={schema}
>
  <p class="doc-binding">
    This English text is provided for convenience and has not been reviewed by a lawyer;
    the legally binding version is the <a href={bgPath} hreflang="bg">Bulgarian original</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>1. Who the other party is</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>{b.legalName}</strong>, a trader operating under the brand {b.name}, {address}.
  </p>
  <dl>
    {b.eik && <><dt>{t.eik} (EIK)</dt><dd>{b.eik}</dd></>}
    <dt>Address for withdrawal and complaints</dt>
    <dd>{address}</dd>
    <dt>Phone</dt>
    <dd><a href={`tel:${b.phone}`}>{b.phoneIntl}</a></dd>
    <dt>Email</dt>
    <dd><a href={`mailto:${b.email}`}>{b.email}</a></dd>
  </dl>

  <h2>2. Right of withdrawal: 14 days</h2>
  <p>
    When the contract is concluded <strong>at a distance</strong> (by phone, through the form on
    the site or by email) or <strong>off business premises</strong>, as a consumer you have the
    right to withdraw within <strong>14 days</strong>, without paying compensation and without
    giving a reason. The legal basis is Article 50 of the Consumer Protection Act (ZZP).
  </p>
  <p>
    For a service, the period runs from the day the contract is concluded. If you have ordered
    goods (a part, for example), it runs from the day you receive them.
  </p>

  <h3>2.1. When the right of withdrawal LAPSES</h3>
  <p>
    This is the most important part, and we state it plainly instead of hiding it in small print.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>The service has been fully performed.</strong> If you asked for the work to start
      before the 14 days were up and it has been completed, the right of withdrawal lapses
      (Article 57, item 1 ZZP). In practice this covers almost every job we do: the car is left
      with us and the file is written the same day.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>The work has started but is not finished.</strong> You can then withdraw, but you
      owe a <strong>proportionate part</strong> of the price for the work already done.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Goods or services made to order.</strong> A file written for the specific ECU of
      your specific car is personalised by its nature.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Before we start work within the 14-day period, we will ask for your <strong>express
    consent</strong> and tell you that once the work has been performed the right of withdrawal
    lapses. Consent is given in writing or on a durable medium, not by silence.
  </p>

  <h3>2.2. How to exercise it</h3>
  <p>
    An unambiguous statement made before the period ends is enough: a letter, an email or the
    completed form. It is up to you to prove that you sent it in time, so we recommend email or
    a letter with proof of delivery.
  </p>
  <p>
    Send it to <a href={`mailto:${b.email}`}>{b.email}</a> or to the address in point 1. We
    confirm receipt without delay.
  </p>

  <h3>2.3. Model withdrawal form</h3>
  <p>Fill it in only if you wish to. Any clear statement does the same job.</p>
  <blockquote class="form-withdrawal">
    <p>To {b.legalName}, {address}, {b.email}</p>
    <p>
      I hereby give notice that I withdraw from my contract for the purchase of the following
      goods / for the provision of the following service: ……………………………………………………
    </p>
    <p>Order number (if any): ………………………</p>
    <p>Ordered on / received on: ………………………</p>
    <p>Name of consumer: ………………………</p>
    <p>Address of consumer: ………………………</p>
    <p>Signature (only if submitted on paper): ………………………</p>
    <p>Date: ………………………</p>
  </blockquote>

  <h3>2.4. Refunds</h3>
  <p>
    We refund the amounts received <strong>within 14 days</strong> of the day we are informed of
    the withdrawal. We refund them by the <strong>same means</strong> you used to pay, unless we
    expressly agree otherwise, and you pay no fee for that.
  </p>
  <p>
    If the work began at your express request, the proportionate part for what has already been
    done is deducted from the amount.
  </p>

  <h3>2.5. Ordering PDK Flasher from the site: the device and the file</h3>
  <p>
    Here the rights split in two, because you are buying two different things. We set this out
    separately because the general text for a service at the workshop does not fit an order
    delivered by courier.
  </p>
  <dl>
    <dt>The PDK Flasher device (goods)</dt>
    <dd>
      <strong>14 days from the day you receive it.</strong> You return it at your own cost, in the
      condition in which you received it. You may examine and try it as you would in a shop; if
      it is damaged or used beyond that, you are liable for the reduced value. We refund the
      payment within 14 days, but may withhold it until we receive the device back or you show
      that you have sent it (Article 55 ZZP).
    </dd>

    <dt>The tuning software (digital content)</dt>
    <dd>
      The file is not supplied on a physical medium. The right of withdrawal for it therefore
      lapses only when <strong>three conditions are met together</strong>: you have given
      <strong>express consent</strong> for preparation to start immediately, you have
      <strong>confirmed</strong> that you thereby lose the right of withdrawal, and
      <strong>performance has begun</strong> (Article 57, item 13 ZZP).
    </dd>

    <dt>If you do NOT give this consent</dt>
    <dd>
      Nothing is lost; we simply wait. We start preparing the file once the 14-day period has
      expired. The device is sent to you straight away, whichever you choose.
    </dd>
  </dl>
  <p>
    Consent is given with a <strong>separate tick box</strong> in the order. It is never
    pre-ticked, and the order goes through without it. Pre-ticked consent is not consent.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you withdraw from the whole package before the file has been prepared, we refund
    everything you paid. If you withdraw after the file has been delivered but
    <strong>without</strong> having consented to immediate performance, we also refund
    everything. If you did consent, we refund the value of the device, not of the software.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Complaints: when the work is not right</h2>
  <p>
    A complaint is something different from withdrawal: you file it when the service does not
    match what was agreed. The legal basis is Article 123 et seq. ZZP.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Deadline:</strong> up to <strong>14 days</strong> from discovering the
      non-conformity, for a service. For goods, the period is up to <strong>2 years</strong> from
      delivery.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>What you can ask for:</strong> first, that the service is performed in line with the
      contract; if that does not happen within a reasonable time, a price reduction or a refund.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>What to attach:</strong> proof of payment (invoice or till receipt), a description of
      the non-conformity and, if there is one, the printout from the dyno.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    A complaint can be filed in person, by phone or at
    <a href={`mailto:${b.email}`}>{b.email}</a>. We enter it in a register and give you a
    document with its number and date. We decide on it within <strong>30 days</strong>.
  </p>

  <h3>3.1. What is not grounds for a complaint</h3>
  <p>
    We state this too, so that there are no surprises either way:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>damage from wear, poor fuel or a missed service;</li>
    <li>later changes to the software by another workshop;</li>
    <li>hardware replaced after our work without our knowledge;</li>
    <li>an authorised dealer refusing to honour the factory warranty. We warn about this
      <strong>before</strong> any work (see the <a href={terms.href}>terms and conditions</a>, point 5.4).</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>3.2. The device and the file bought from the site</h3>
  <p>
    For these we are liable under the <strong>Act on the Provision of Digital Content and
    Digital Services and on the Sale of Goods</strong>, not under the general rules for a
    workshop service.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>The device:</strong> we are liable for any non-conformity that becomes apparent
      within <strong>2 years</strong> of delivery. During the first year, the non-conformity is
      presumed to have existed at delivery unless we prove otherwise. We first repair or replace
      it; if that does not happen within a reasonable time and without significant inconvenience
      to you, we reduce the price or refund the payment.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>The software:</strong> we are responsible for the file working with the car it was
      made for. If it will not write, will not start, or the car does not achieve what was
      described, we fix it or refund what you paid for it.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Delivery:</strong> if the parcel arrives damaged, have it noted with the courier
      when you receive it and call us the same day. A photo of the packaging helps more than a
      long letter.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>4. Cancelling a booked appointment</h2>
  <p>
    This is neither withdrawal nor a complaint, just an arrangement between people. If you
    cannot come, call us. The dyno and the work bay are reserved for you, and an empty slot is
    lost for both sides. We do not charge for a cancelled appointment.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Disputes</h2>
  <p>
    If we cannot reach agreement, you can refer the matter to the <strong>Commission for
    Consumer Protection (KZP)</strong>, 4A Slaveykov Sq., Sofia 1000, tel. 0700 111 22,
    <a href="https://kzp.bg/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">kzp.bg</a>.
  </p>
  <p>
    For alternative dispute resolution, the competent bodies are the
    <strong>conciliation committees at the KZP</strong>:
    <a href="https://kzp.bg/pomiritelna-komisiya" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">kzp.bg/pomiritelna-komisiya</a>.
    The full terms are in the <a href={terms.href}>terms and conditions</a>, point 13.
  </p>
</Text>

<style is:global>
/* The binding-version note opens the body. */
.doc-body .doc-binding{color:var(--ink-3);font-style:italic}

/* The withdrawal form: it should read as a template to fill in, not as running text. */
.form-withdrawal{margin:0 0 22px;padding:22px 24px;border-left:2px solid var(--lime);
  background:var(--lime-dim);border-radius:0 var(--r-s) var(--r-s) 0}
/* The blanks are one long UNBREAKABLE run of dots. At 320px it pushed the document
   to 330px wide. `anywhere` allows a break inside the run without splitting words. */
.form-withdrawal p{margin:0 0 12px;font:400 var(--fz-s)/1.75 var(--body);color:var(--ink-2);
  overflow-wrap:anywhere}
.form-withdrawal p:last-child{margin-bottom:0}
</style>
